sh","facts":[{"key":"no_external_debt","value":"Council is debt-free; had no borrowing requirement during 2025/26 and remains debt free","as_at":"2026-03-31","source":{"title":"Annual Treasury Management Report for 2025/26 \u2014 Council Executive, 22 July 2026","url":"https://moderngov.erewash.gov.uk/documents/s42783/annual-treasury-management-outturn-2526v2.pdf","doc_id":42783,"drive_id":null,"text":"papers/E07000036/42783.txt"},"note":"\u00a73.18 (p.4) verbatim: 'The Council had no borrowing requirement during the year 2025/26 and remains debt free.' Our PWLB price book returns no borrower on any variant of Erewash (queried 15 August 2026). Ties on both sides."},{"key":"cfr","value":"Opening \u00a30m, closing \u00a30m; unfinanced capex added and MRP charged in year (both printed as '\u00a3173' with an '\u00a3m' column header \u2014 see internal note)","as_at":"2026-03-31","source":{"title":"Annual Treasury Management Report for 2025/26 \u2014 Council Executive, 22 July 2026","url":"https://moderngov.erewash.gov.uk/documents/s42783/annual-treasury-management-outturn-2526v2.pdf","doc_id":42783,"drive_id":null,"text":"papers/E07000036/42783.txt"},"note":"\u00a73.17 table (p.4). The '\u00a3m' column header is inconsistent with \u00a73.12 capex (\u00a39.927m fully financed by grants/receipts/reserves) and with \u00a73.16 attributing the movement to IFRS 16 lease recognition \u2014 almost certainly the '\u00a3173' is \u00a3173k. Not raiseable. Closing CFR is 0 as printed."},{"key":"capital_expenditure","value":"\u00a39.927m actual spend in 2025/26, financed entirely by capital grants, receipts and reserves; nothing to borrowing","as_at":"2026-03-31","source":{"title":"Annual Treasury Management Report for 2025/26 \u2014 Council Executive, 22 July 2026","url":"https://moderngov.erewash.gov.uk/documents/s42783/annual-treasury-management-outturn-2526v2.pdf","doc_id":42783,"drive_id":null,"text":"papers/E07000036/42783.txt"},"note":"\u00a73.12 table (p.3). Revised estimate \u00a310.477m vs original \u00a324.628m \u2014 significant slippage explained at \u00a73.7(b) as delays on Towns Fund projects."},{"key":"investment_book","value":"\u00a323.475m of investments at 31 March 2026 (per \u00a73.4 text); sector breakdown in the same paragraph sums to \u00a329.919m (Banking \u00a3419k, DMO \u00a321.500m, Other LAs \u00a38.000m)","as_at":"2026-03-31","source":{"title":"Annual Treasury Management Report for 2025/26 \u2014 Council Executive, 22 July 2026","url":"https://moderngov.erewash.gov.uk/documents/s42783/annual-treasury-management-outturn-2526v2.pdf","doc_id":42783,"drive_id":null,"text":"papers/E07000036/42783.txt"},"note":"\u00a73.4 (p.2). The two totals in the same paragraph do not reconcile \u2014 recorded verbatim. See papers/E07000036/42783.txt for the internal-only observation; not raiseable. Detail sits in Appendix 1 which is not held in this covering PDF."},{"key":"investment_rate","value":"4.092% average return on \u00a331.037m average internally managed balance in 2025/26; \u00a31.396m interest received against a \u00a31.200m budget (fav variance \u00a3196k)","as_at":"2026-03-31","source":{"title":"Annual Treasury Management Report for 2025/26 \u2014 Council Executive, 22 July 2026","url":"https://moderngov.erewash.gov.uk/documents/s42783/annual-treasury-management-outturn-2526v2.pdf","doc_id":42783,"drive_id":null,"text":"papers/E07000036/42783.txt"},"note":"\u00a73.4 and \u00a73.6-3.7 (p.2). Derived check \u00a331.037m \u00d7 4.092% \u2248 \u00a31.270m, within reach of the \u00a31.396m received (difference explained by intra-year balance movement and accrual). Variance attributed at \u00a73.7 to rates not being cut as forecast and Towns Fund slippage keeping cash balances higher for longer."},{"key":"investment_performance","value":"SONIA vs Council: 7d 3.73% vs 3.56% (under 17bp); 1m 3.74% vs 4.16%; 3m 3.75% vs 4.00%; 1y 3.95% vs 4.27%","as_at":"2026-03-31","source":{"title":"Annual Treasury Management Report for 2025/26 \u2014 Council Executive, 22 July 2026","url":"https://moderngov.erewash.gov.uk/documents/s42783/annual-treasury-management-outturn-2526v2.pdf","doc_id":42783,"drive_id":null,"text":"papers/E07000036/42783.txt"},"note":"\u00a73.8 table (p.2). The table header prints 'year ended 31 March 2025' inside a 2025/26 outturn report \u2014 a template typo. Not raiseable. Overall the council beat SONIA on the 1-month / 3-month / 1-year buckets and slightly underperformed on 7-day."},{"key":"prudential_compliance","value":"Council operated within all treasury and prudential indicators during the year ended 31 March 2026; detail sits in Appendix 3 which is not held","as_at":"2026-03-31","source":{"title":"Annual Treasury Management Report for 2025/26 \u2014 Council Executive, 22 July 2026","url":"https://moderngov.erewash.gov.uk/documents/s42783/annual-treasury-management-outturn-2526v2.pdf","doc_id":42783,"drive_id":null,"text":"papers/E07000036/42783.txt"},"note":"\u00a73.11 (p.3). No indicator values are printed in the covering paper."},{"key":"financing_costs_to_net_revenue","value":"Not applicable \u2014 Council is debt-free, so there are no financing costs. Not reported in this paper.","as_at":"2026-03-31","source":{"title":"Annual Treasury Management Report for 2025/26 \u2014 Council Executive, 22 July 2026","url":"https://moderngov.erewash.gov.uk/documents/s42783/annual-treasury-management-outturn-2526v2.pdf","doc_id":42783,"drive_id":null,"text":"papers/E07000036/42783.txt"},"note":"The indicator measures net financing costs against Net Revenue Stream. Erewash has no external debt; \u00a73.18 confirms this."}],"threads":[],"meetings":{},"summary":{"written":"15 August 2026","text":"<p>Erewash carries no external debt. \u00a73.18 (p.4) is verbatim: 'The Council had no borrowing requirement during the year 2025/26 and remains debt free.' Our PWLB price book returns no borrower on any variant of the name. Both sides tie: nothing to reconcile because there is nothing there.</p><p>The paper is short and the investment book is modest. Average internally managed balance \u00a331.037m at 4.092%; year-end position stated as \u00a323.475m in the text of \u00a73.4, with the sector table in the same paragraph adding to \u00a329.919m across the DMO (\u00a321.500m), other local authorities (\u00a38.000m) and a working bank balance (\u00a3419k). Investment interest \u00a31.396m against a \u00a31.200m budget, with the variance attributed to rates holding up better than forecast and to Towns Fund capital slippage keeping cash balances higher for longer. Performance sat above SONIA on the 1-month, 3-month and 1-year buckets and 17bp below on 7-day.</p><p>The Capital Financing Requirement opens and closes at zero, with \u00a73.17 recording only movement tied to IFRS 16 lease recognition. Capital expenditure of \u00a39.927m in the year (\u00a73.12) was financed entirely by grants, receipts and reserves \u2014 nothing fell to borrowing. \u00a73.11 records compliance with all treasury and prudential indicators; the detail sits in Appendix 3 which is not attached to the covering PDF we hold.</p><p><b>Thin for our purposes. No email drafted.</b> This is a debt-free district with a small, mostly-DMO investment book, no LOBOs, no maturity profile to talk about and no distinctive investment shape (contrast Chichester, where a \u00a351m LA-lending position and a 227-day duration profile gave us something to say). None of the four EMAIL_TEMPLATE.md \u00a76 hook tests apply: no dated testable assumption, no distinctive position, no unusual detail we could compliment specifically, no cross-council pattern the paper connects to. A thin note is a correct outcome and better than a padded email.</p>"},"courses":{"scored":false,"read":["treasury_annual"],"text_held":true},"contacts":[{"name":"Judy Fay","role":"Chief Accountant","email":"judy.fay@erewash.gov.uk","note":"Contact officer on doc 42783 (p.5) with address and phone (0115 907 1054). Title verbatim from the paper. NOT identified in the paper as Section 151 Officer \u2014 do not address as such."},{"name":"Lisa Dudley","role":"Group Accountant","email":"lisa.dudley@erewash.gov.uk","note":"Contact officer on doc 42783 (p.5) with address and phone (0115 907 1059). Title verbatim from the paper."},{"name":null,"role":"Director of Resources (Section 151 Officer)","email":null,"note":"The report is styled on the cover as 'Report of the Director of Resources to the Council Executive' but the officer is not named in this paper. Do not guess."}],"status":{"state":"read-thin","written_up":true,"contact":true,"as_at":"15 August 2026","source_text_held":true,"note":"Read from local PDF. Paper text at papers/E07000036/42783.txt. PWLB reconciliation TIES: price book returns no borrower on any variant of Erewash, and \u00a73.18 confirms debt-free position; nothing to reconcile because there is nothing there. Balance-sheet identity trivially satisfied: CFR 0 - external 0 - other LTL (IFRS 16 lease, undisclosed here) = internal 0 \u00b1 lease. NO EMAIL DRAFTED \u2014 the paper is thin from an outreach angle: debt-free small district, small mostly-DMO investment book, nothing distinctive against sector or against the paper's own reference points. Internal-only observations (two investment totals that don't reconcile inside \u00a73.4, a header typo at \u00a73.8, and a probable \u00a3m/\u00a3k unit error at \u00a73.17) are recorded in the extract file but MUST NOT be raised with the council."},"emails":{}}}